      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Noturus crypticus Burr, Eisenhour &amp; Grady, 2005</li><li>Common name: Chucky Madtom</li><li>IUCN Red List: Critically Endangered (last assessed 2012)</li><li>Breeding: unreported</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1222",
      "html": "<p>North America: USA. Gulf Coast Drainages, Mississippi, Ohio, Tennessee, French Broad. Type locality: Little Chucky Creek at mouth of Jackson Branch, Greene County, Tennessee, U.S.A.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1222",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1222",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: from the Greek notos, meaning back, and oura, meaning tail, in reference to the confluent adipose and caudal fins. The epithet crypticus has two possible meanings: the first refers to its nocturnal ways, the second to this species keeping its identity a secret from researchers for so long.</p>"
    },
